#hash((content-digest . "fd18914ee58e8c060e657addfc5540b9df57937538d9604936b4a4ecbb4f0dfd") (milestone . 896) (plan-id . "fb67e0429ed155a4b4e3f31afe3ef3ca7748ee891c06247b11e5e2a86cfebd75") (report . "Three rounds were completed and all three returned CHANGES-REQUESTED. All twelve findings were reproduced against the tree before any fix was written, and every one is fixed with its own evidence: the W2 gate repair carries a red-first capture showing the previously masked failure now reaches the gate, the prose corrections are diffs against the artifacts they cite, and the two round-3 substantiation findings are re-measurements rather than restatements - the sweep was genuinely re-run and the checksums genuinely re-verified in full. The pattern across the rounds is consistent: each round found the same class of defect one step further along, in the claim that pointed at the evidence rather than in the evidence itself, which is why rounds 2 and 3 returned findings of the same shape as round 1's. Round 4 is pending. No value in this record is invented, and this record does not assert approval.") (reviewed-sha . "86002515f9de49d4abd83d83fd279656ab7c15e7") (reviewer . "independent read-only VERIFY subagents (reviewer role), 4 rounds solicited") (rounds . (#hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R1-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. The W2 checks are now a test-suite run through run-tests whose returned failure count drives (exit 1), so failed-result? sees a non-zero exit. The W2 overlap review and SHA256SUMS are pinned to the frozen v1.00.29 campaign; the W0 ownership matrix stays derived so the checks double as a live drift check (both matrices have identical overlap scope: 34 platform/fast, 46 security/fast). Red-first proof at raw/red-first-worker-security-w2.txt: with the W2 path pointed at a nonexistent directory the file now exits 1 and the runner reports FAILED, where the identical broken state before the fix reported PASSED (33/33, exit 0).") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "tests/test-worker-security.rkt derived its W2 overlap artifact paths from q-version (naming artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.31-w2, which does not exist) and could not fail the gate, so the regression was invisible")) #hash((id . "R1-F2") (resolution . "FIXED. CHANGELOG and the release report name the matrix's actual values and say why they moved (the bake's own derivation sweep changed two of the nine digest-bound inputs, so the matrix was regenerated by its canonical generator).") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "W6 PERMANENT prose bound the verdict to the superseded rehearsal identity (head fc1a6fa36, inputs digest a1b99fe2) while the committed matrix records 50bdf7334 / fb224a6f")) #hash((id . "R1-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. Both passages now state six of seven gates pass and that readiness is deferred, not passed, with the reason (branch-gated; its .gate-evidence records must name the release commit and version).") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The changelog claimed every release-preflight gate passes locally and listed readiness among them, while release-preflight.json records readiness as deferred-by-design")) #hash((id . "R1-F4") (resolution . "PARTIALLY FIXED in round 1, completed in round 3. The checksum step was corrected to run from the repo root and a single capture retained per gate; head coherence is stated precisely rather than claimed. Round 3 judged the form correct but the substantiation incomplete, which became R3-F4.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "W7 evidence was not coherently bound: the preflight named the first bake commit, the preflight JSON a later commit, and the verify chain an intermediate one, and that chain recorded a failed checksum run caused by executing sha256sum -c from inside the artifact directory")))) (reviewed-sha . "55abf0271f61ae4797881c64d3948834cc5c1d7e") (round . 1) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R2-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. The entry now records both re-stamps and names the current committed values as authoritative.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "w4-recovery.json still described the W6 matrix as re-stamped to fc1a6fa36 with byte-identical inputs, contradicting the regeneration this bake performed")) #hash((id . "R2-F2") (resolution . "PARTIALLY FIXED in round 2, completed in round 3. The report was corrected to the then-current preflight head, but round 3 found the same class of defect one step further along: the preflight was later re-run at b0f19d6bd while the report and the validation record still said 58d302db. Both now name b0f19d6bd, the head the retained capture names.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The release report quoted the first bake commit fcfa9ab3 and 84 changed .rkt files while the retained preflight capture recorded a later commit and 93")) #hash((id . "R2-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. The 1511 value is consistent across the report, the preflight JSON, the validation record and the chain capture.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The report quoted 1510 test files scanned for the version-expectation lint; the real count is 1511")) #hash((id . "R2-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The claim is replaced by the precise account: each capture names the tree it ran against; the commits between the suite chain (e9af72fee) and the content head change only docs/reports prose and this directory's own JSON and raw captures, which no test reads; and git diff --name-only e9af72fee..86002515f confirms no source or test file changed after the chain ran, so the chain's numbers describe the merge candidate's code.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "release-preflight.json claimed the three captures were 'all bound to the same content head', which was false - a committed artifact cannot contain the SHA of the commit that carries it")))) (reviewed-sha . "21b753a26595be03db432f8a046efd0a97a6876a") (round . 2) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R3-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. Both now name b0f19d6bd.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The release report and the validation record still attributed the preflight to 58d302db while the retained preflight artifacts (release-preflight.json and raw/preflight-locally-runnable.txt) both record b0f19d6bd. The previous fix had chased the moving commit one step and stopped short.")) #hash((id . "R3-F2") (resolution . "FIXED. The sweep was re-run at the final head - 19 files, 0 failures, 0 errors - and the new capture states in its own header what it supersedes and why. The reviewer also observed that raco test exits 0 even when a case fails, so the per-file rackunit counts rather than the exit code are the signal; that is recorded in the preflight JSON, and it is the same failure mode that hid the worker-security W2 regression.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "release-preflight.json claimed 0 failures, 0 errors citing raw/version-derivation-tests.log, but that capture was taken mid-repair and records test-wave-integrity-adversarial.rkt red (1/8) while the W6 matrix was still pinned to the pre-regeneration identity. The claim was true and the evidence under it was not.")) #hash((id . "R3-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. Head, counts and elapsed time now match the capture they cite; the fast-suite duration (20m51s to 20m53s) was corrected in the same pass, and a raw-captures block now names which file substantiates which number.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The validation record quoted a full regression at 1935c2c90 with 20548 of 20549 tests and 29m40s while citing raw/verify-chain.txt, which records e9af72fee with 20553 of 20554 and 29m36s - an earlier run's numbers under a later run's filename.")) #hash((id . "R3-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The full unfiltered per-manifest output is retained in the chain capture: 6/6 W6, 9/9 W7, 1/1 tier-ownership, 16/16 entries, run from the repository root. It is retained there rather than in a sidecar log because the artifact-provenance linter requires every file under the wave artifact directory to be bound by SHA256SUMS. The single unavoidable self-reference is stated in the log, the report and the preflight JSON: the manifest entry for the log covers the log including the checksum section, so the log cannot verify its own entry.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The chain's checksum section showed three OK lines for manifests holding sixteen entries, so its all-OK summary was unsubstantiated by its own excerpt.")) #hash((id . "R3-NB") (resolution . "Accepted as accurate. The 1510 in the red-first capture is labelled rather than edited, because rewriting a red-first capture to match a later run would destroy the red/green pair it exists to record. The reviewer independently confirmed sound: the runner base-dir tests (non-vacuous, each building a decoy q/ fixture, and now counted by the runner), all eight frozen-path pins and both authoring-identity pins with truthful comments, the readiness-deferred wording, the W6 PERMANENT and W4 DELIVERED bounding, the absence of any PR-check substitution, and the playwright-sidecar environmental claim (@requires browser at the file, ci profile skips it, identical failure on main).") (severity . "non-blocking") (summary . "Round 3's non-blocking observations: the superseded red-first capture's 1510 count, a confusing runner taxonomy label in the W2 red-first record, and prose drift in one suite duration.")) #hash((id . "R3-TOOL") (resolution . "Recorded so the round's scope is not overstated. Its findings were all verified independently against the tree before any fix was written, and all four were real.") (severity . "process") (summary . "Round 3 ran without an exec tool in the child process, so it could not recompute the content digest, run git diff, verify checksums or execute tests, and marked those unverified.")))) (reviewed-sha . "9ff617f2c73f7207fd6fd73077b16dcfd3996823 (chain head e9af72fee)") (round . 3) (rounds-prior-fix-check . "Six of the eight prior findings confirmed GENUINELY FIXED: R1-F1 (the W2 checks now run through run-tests whose failure count drives the exit; the frozen v1.00.29 artifacts verified on disk and self-identifying; the red-first capture consistent at 33-before/38-after with exactly the three artifact-reading cases failing), R1-F2 (the strict-runner assertion now requires both the strict variable and a run-tests.rkt invocation, checked against ci.yml's fast, platform and security windows; a lane dropping strictness cannot satisfy it), R1-F3 (no stale fc1a6fa36/a1b99fe2 identity survives in the release surface - the remaining mentions are legitimate history), R2-F1 (w4-recovery.json records both re-stamps and matches the committed matrix field-for-field), R2-F3 (1511 everywhere in the release surface), and R1-F4's checksum path. R1-F4 was accepted as fixed in form but left substantiation incomplete, which became R3-F4. R2-F2 was judged NOT FIXED and became R3-F1.") (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . ()) (note . "Round 4 is to confirm rounds 1-3's twelve findings at this head and run a fresh adversarial pass. Until it returns APPROVED, this wave is not merge-authorized.") (reviewed-sha . "86002515f9de49d4abd83d83fd279656ab7c15e7") (round . 4) (verdict . "PENDING - not yet run")))) (schema-version . 2) (scope . "W7 blocked-wave repair, bake and v1.00.31 release, reviewed read-only against the frozen W7 wave doc in the campaign plan snapshot. Rounds 1-3 covered the runner base-dir fix and its regression tests, the three classes of version-coincidence defect, the W2 gate-integrity repair and its red-first proof, the W6 rehearsal matrix regeneration and head re-stamp, the W4 local-capture correction, the release honesty of the CHANGELOG entry and the release report, and the coherence and substantiation of the W7 evidence captures. Each round was a fresh read-only reviewer at the then-current head; no finding was accepted without being reproduced against the tree first.") (timestamp . "2026-09-25T17:10:00Z (r1) / 2026-09-25T17:35:00Z (r2) / 2026-09-25T20:20:00Z (r3)") (tooling-notes . "Round 3 was obtained on a later attempt: the first two attempts failed with a provider usage-limit error on the reviewer role's default model, an OpenRouter credit limit (402) on an alternative, and an OpenRouter monthly key limit (403) on a third. No verdict was invented in place of those failures; the attempt that did run produced the findings recorded above.") (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED (rounds 1, 2 and 3; all twelve findings verified and fixed); round 4 PENDING - NOT APPROVED, and this record must not be read as approval"))
